@@ -314,6 +314,14 @@ done patch-agent chat is hidden from the left pane and the command interface bec
 the user types later chat while that done feature is the most recently closed session, the terminal
 adapter restores the session, selects it, and routes the chat back through `WorkLeafController`.
 
+Command mode also supports Vim-style visual selections in the focused pane. `v`, `V`, and `Ctrl-V`
+start character, line, and block selections; `h`, `j`, `k`, `l`, and terminal arrow sequences move
+the selection cursor; `y` copies the selected range; and `Y` copies linewise text. Copied text is
+drained by the terminal adapter and emitted once as an OSC52 clipboard sequence on the next rendered
+frame. Visual selection input stays inside the active selection, so slash keys and escape-prefixed
+arrow bytes do not start selected-agent slash commands or chat-history navigation while visual mode
+is active.
+
 `src/ui.rs::TerminalUi` owns terminal-specific presentation state:
 
 - `UiMode`, `PaneFocus`, `UiSurface`, `UiKey`, and `UiAction` model terminal interactions.
@@ -321,11 +329,14 @@ adapter restores the session, selects it, and routes the chat back through `Work
 - `TerminalLayout` computes pane geometry.
 - `TerminalUi` renders left/right panes, prompts, cursor placement, command-interface selection, and
   terminal navigation actions. The right pane keeps the chat prompt visible while scroll offsets
-  reveal earlier transcript rows.
+  reveal earlier transcript rows. Visual selection state and copied text are terminal presentation
+  concerns owned by `TerminalUi`.
 
 `src/ui_harness.rs::UiHarness` is the test harness for terminal behavior. It exercises the same
 `TerminalUi` frame path used by the interactive example. UI tests should drive
 `UiHarness::handle_byte` or `UiHarness::handle_bytes` rather than duplicating terminal input logic.
+The harness records drained copied text so visual selection tests can assert copy results without
+depending on terminal OSC52 support.
 
 A web UI, desktop UI, or non-terminal integration should not depend on `TerminalApp` or
 `TerminalUi`; it should depend on `WorkLeafController` and the DTOs in `src/workspace.rs`.
